On 12/05/2015 17:30, And Rosta wrote:
>
> On 12 May 2015 12:57, "Spheniscine (la zipcpi)" <spheniscine@gmail.com 
> <mailto:spheniscine@gmail.com>> wrote:
> > {ua je'e} Well, I'd still strongly prefer for it to be 
> monosyllabic... perhaps {iau}?
>
> There are lots of cmavo one would prefer to be monosyllabic, with 
> vau'u far from the top of the list, and the BPFK will need to decide 
> firstly whether to recycle any formerly assigned monosyllabic cmavo 
> and secondly which available monosyllabic cmavo forms to assign to 
> which candidate functions.
>
> Until that happens, you should always choose a disyllabic experimental 
> cmavo so that its usage frequency isn't distorted by its temporary 
> monosyllabicity.
>
Agreed. The number of monosyllabic cmavo is very limited, and should 
ideally be reserved for the most frequently needed functions. The 
Korpora zei Sisku is a suitable tool for figuring out which cmavo or 
cmavo compounds are most used, and thus best candidates for monosyllabicity.

mi'e la .ilmen. mu'o


